codex
All three regressions were RED against `720303d`: both backdated shapes raised `OBSERVATION_SUPERSESSION_INVALID`, and the conditional poison escaped the batch before the healthy run. The fix now uses the pinned harvest/reconciliation clock for observation ordering, retains the true resolver timestamp in evidence, reuses one hashed snapshot across STARTED and writes, isolates batch failures, and caps consecutive retries at three. Typecheck is already clean; I’m running the database regressions next.
